// =============================================================================
// inspections-course — "Inspections: What You Look At Before You Sign"
// =============================================================================
// Course TEN of the Real Estate department. Nine courses covered the ground,
// the stewardship, the transaction, the tenant, the building, the partner, the
// lender, the record and the loss. This one covers the act every one of them
// depends on and none of them teaches: LOOKING at a thing properly before you
// are bound to it.
//
// THE ARC, one argument in eight moves:
//   1. The plague in the walls    (Leviticus 14:33-45)
//   2. I viewed the walls         (Nehemiah 2:11-18)
//   3. See the land, what it is   (Numbers 13:17-20)
//   4. Two reports, one land      (Numbers 13:25-33; 14:6-9, 24)
//   5. They came to search it out (Joshua 2:1-6, 23-24)
//   6. Man looketh on the outward appearance (1 Samuel 16:6, 7; John 7:24)
//   7. He digged deep             (Luke 6:46-49; Isaiah 28:16, 17)
//   8. Prove all things           (1 Thessalonians 5:21; Acts 17:11; 1 John 4:1;
//                                  2 Kings 22:3-7)
//
// Get the whole inspection PROCEDURE from Yahweh's own hand -> learn to look
// before you announce -> get the checklist He wrote for men He sent to survey a
// country -> find out exactly where an honest report turns into an evil one ->
// see a second look taken with a different aim -> learn what the eye cannot
// reach -> put the foundation above the finish -> and end on the habit
// generalising, and on the record so consistent that reckoning stopped.
//
// THE FIND THIS COURSE IS BUILT ON, and it is startling. Leviticus 14:33-45 is
// a COMPLETE, STAGED BUILDING INSPECTION, written by Yahweh, with every element
// a modern protocol has and one most of them lack:
//
//   * the OWNER reports a suspicion, not a diagnosis -- "It seemeth to me there
//     is as it were a plague in the house" (14:35)
//   * EMPTY THE HOUSE BEFORE THE INSPECTOR GOES IN, and the reason is given:
//     "that all that is in the house be not made unclean" (14:36). The
//     inspection is designed so it cannot condemn the contents by happening.
//   * stated visible CRITERIA -- "hollow strakes, greenish or reddish, which in
//     sight are lower than the wall" (14:37)
//   * a WAITING PERIOD and a SECOND LOOK -- shut it up seven days, and "the
//     priest shall come again the seventh day, and shall look" (14:38, 39),
//     because a spreading defect and a static one are not the same defect
//   * TARGETED remediation with disposal away from the site (14:40, 41, 42)
//   * a RE-INSPECTION after the repair (14:43, 44)
//   * and a STOPPING RULE: if it returns after all of that, the house comes
//     down (14:45)
//
// A household that ran only those seven steps on a building would be ahead of
// most buyers alive.
//
// THE FOUR LIMITS THIS COURSE HOLDS, each a place the material is easily
// abused, and each pinned by the course test rather than trusted to prose:
//
//   Leviticus 14 -- this is Yahweh's law about ritual uncleanness, and the text
//     says plainly "I put the plague of leprosy in a house" (14:34). It is NOT
//     a building code, and it must never be turned into "damp walls are a
//     judgment on you." What carries is the PROCEDURE, which is His and is
//     wise; the theology of why a particular house had it is His business and
//     the text does not hand it to us.
//   Numbers 13 -- the ten were NOT punished for reporting the facts. Their
//     facts were accurate: strong people, walled cities, the children of Anak.
//     What Scripture calls an evil report is the addition in 13:32 and the
//     conclusion drawn in unbelief -- and Caleb never denied the giants. Honest
//     measurement is required; despair wearing measurement's clothes is not.
//   1 Samuel 16:7 -- "man looketh on the outward appearance" is about Yahweh
//     choosing a king. It is not a reason to skip looking at a foundation, and
//     anyone using it that way has inverted it.
//   Joshua 2 -- the Word records Rahab's words to the king's men and commends
//     her faith elsewhere without commenting on them. This course teaches what
//     the passage shows -- men were sent, they looked, they reported briefly
//     and truly -- and stays where Scripture stays on the rest.
//
// FRESHNESS, MEASURED (DR-0076 sec.4), and the measurement killed three planned
// lessons before a word of them was written. Ezekiel 13's untempered morter is
// already the anchor of maint3, Proverbs 20:14's "it is naught, it is naught"
// is already buy3, and Haggai's "consider your ways" is already maint6 -- all
// inside this same department. Every chapter here was checked against the
// department's own mounted text BEFORE authoring, which is the order course
// nine learned the hard way when its own header claim went stale mid-build.
//
// What is true, measured against the nine other mounted Real Estate courses:
// this course cites 53 verses and NOT ONE of them is cited anywhere else in
// that department. ONE chapter is shared, at a different verse -- Proverbs 14
// (here :15, the simple and the prudent; maintenance-trades at :4 and :23, the
// ox and the labour). The course test pins the verse-level claim so it cannot
// rot.
//
// BANDS, BENEFITS AND STORIES FROM THE FIRST COMMIT (DR-0509), every hard term
// leads with its plain meaning (DR-0521), and every quoted span is verbatim
// from the repository's own KJV with its own reference and no ellipsis
// (DR-0459). Our prose says Yahweh; quotations keep "God" and "the LORD"
// exactly as the KJV has them (DR-0210).
//
// TEACHING, NOT INSPECTION, LEGAL OR ENGINEERING ADVICE -- carried on the meta.
// =============================================================================

